## Consensus Rules

### Byzantine Fault Tolerance Model

```
Total Agents: 3
Required Agreement: 2 (majority)
Fault Tolerance: 1 agent can fail/disagree
```

### Delegation Validation

For a delegation to be valid, at least 2 of 3 agents must:
1. Verify the delegation token hash matches
2. Confirm the task is within scope
3. Agree the delegation is legitimate

```
Agent 1 (Coordinator) ──► Creates delegation
Agent 2 (Validator 1) ──► Validates ──┐
Agent 3 (Validator 2) ──► Validates ──┼──► 2/3 agree? ──► PROCEED
                                      │
                                      └──► Disagree? ──► FLAG FOR HUMAN
```

### Consensus Outcomes

| Outcome | Votes | Action |
|---------|-------|--------|
| **Unanimous** | 3/3 agree | Proceed with high confidence |
| **Majority** | 2/3 agree | Proceed, log dissent |
| **Split** | 1/3 or 0/3 | HALT, escalate to human |

---

## Scope Boundaries

### Permitted (Within Trinity)

| Operation | Scope | Notes |
|-----------|-------|-------|
| Task delegation | Within Trinity members | Coordinator to validators |
| File operations | Project directories | As defined per agent |
| Consensus requests | Any agent | For validation |
| Status updates | Shared state files | Coordination |

### Prohibited (Require Human)

| Operation | Reason |
|-----------|--------|
| Add Trinity member | Changes trust boundary |
| Remove Trinity member | Changes trust boundary |
| Modify authority grant | Only human can change |
| Expand scope | Only human can grant |
| External delegations | Outside Trinity boundary |

